  "body": "# Gaoxy 0.13.1\n\nPlug applications and middleware can set legacy connection-specific response\nheaders without turning HTTP/2 SSE responses into HTTP 500. The Plug adapter\nremoves these headers, including fields named by `Connection`, before H2/H3\nresponse serialization. Buffered, file, streaming and informational responses\nuse the same compatibility policy.\n\nOrdinary headers and payloads are preserved. HTTP/1 response behavior and strict\nnative response/header and framing validation remain in effect. The native\nWebSocket persistence and capacity defaults introduced in 0.13.0 are unchanged.\n\nAll six Hex distributions and the standalone application use version `0.13.1`.\nSee the [issue 18 plan](../plans/issue-18-plug-response-headers.md) and the\n[release acceptance](../acceptance/release-0.13.1.md) for verification and source\nidentity.\n",
  "created_at": "2026-10-28T16:34:21Z",
